# Copy this file to .env and set the value below. Never commit .env.
#
# GATSBY_INTERNAL_LINKS_PASSWORD is the password for the client-side gate on /internal/.
# - It is NOT a secret. Gatsby inlines every GATSBY_-prefixed variable into the public
#   JavaScript bundle, so anyone can read it from the deployed site. Do not reuse a
#   password that protects anything else.
# - The gate is a convenience screen only: the gated pages are still published as
#   static files.
# - If the variable is unset or empty at build time, /internal/ stays locked for
#   everyone (the gate fails closed).
# - gatsby-config.js also loads .env.<NODE_ENV> (for example .env.development), and a
#   value there takes precedence over this file.
GATSBY_INTERNAL_LINKS_PASSWORD=
